# Topology and CIDOC CRM measuring of :wd_Q5907540 (Amin-Abad / Aminabad)
# from Pascal Coste's PL. LXVI in Monuments modernes de la Perse (Morel, 1867).
# Raster: images/plans/amin_abad.png (mid-resolution colour plate).
# Load with data/wikidata-iran-caravanserais.ttl and data/unesco-1668.ttl.
# UNESCO :amin_abad stays the harvest stub; skos:exactMatch wd:Q5907540.
# Do not hand-edit the harvest files. Do not reuse UNESCO propertyAreaHectare.
#
# Legend keys 1–11. Instance grain: each closed room with a distinct neighbour
# set is its own bot:Space. Repeated keys use a series bot:Zone that
# containsZone the instances. North at the top (B); entrance on the south.
# Octagon is flat-topped: cardinal faces N E S W; diagonal faces NE SE SW NW.
# Hujra (7) index: cardinal faces N/S west→east, E/W north→south; NW diagonal
# inner rooms north-east→south-west. Coste labels 7 on the NW diagonal inner
# ring; NE/SE/SW diagonals show stable stalls there and are not minted as 7.
# Coste 9 is minted only where the numeral is printed (west and north).
# Coste 10 is minted only on towers that carry the numeral (west half).

:Reading_Coste_Aminabad a prov:Activity ;
    rdfs:label "Reading of Pascal Coste's Amin-Abad plan (legend keys 1–11)"@en ;
    prov:used :coste_1867_aminabad ;
    dcterms:source <https://w3id.org/persian-caravanserai-kg/images/plans/amin_abad.png> .

:coste_1867_aminabad a persarch:PlanImage , crm:E31_Document , crm:E73_Information_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Caravanserail Amin-Abad — Pascal Coste, 1867, PL. LXVI"@en ;
